{"name":"Amazon","hex":"#387b54","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Amazon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of a mythical race of female warriors inhabiting the Black Sea area, now usually archaeologically associated with Scythian or Sarmatian female warriors.","A female warrior."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A river in South America, that flows through Brazil for about 4000 miles to the Atlantic.","A region including much of this river; specifically, the region of the Amazon Rainforest, or of the Amazon River Basin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Amazon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Amazon (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Amazon.com, Inc. is an American multinational conglomerate engaged in e-commerce, retail, cloud computing, online advertising, digital streaming, entertainment, and artificial intelligence. Founded in 1994 by Jeff Bezos in Bellevue, Washington, the company started as an online book marketplace that gradually expanded to include virtually all consumer products as well as many other categories, positioned as \"The Everything Store\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg/330px-Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_(company)","wikidata":"Q3884"},{"title":"Amazon rainforest","blocks":[{"text":"The Amazon rainforest, also called the Amazon jungle, Amazonia, or simply the Amazon, is a moist broadleaf tropical rainforest in the Amazon biome that covers most of the Amazon basin of South America. This basin encompasses 7 million km2 (2.7 million sq mi), of which 6 million km2 (2.3 million sq mi) are covered by the rainforest. This region includes territory belonging to nine nations and 3,344 indigenous territories."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Amazon17_%285641020319%29.jpg/330px-Amazon17_%285641020319%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_rainforest","wikidata":"Q177567"},{"title":"Jungle green","blocks":[{"text":"Jungle green is a color that is a rich tone of medium spring green."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle_green","wikidata":"Q373658"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg/500px-Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg/1280px-Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg/500px-Amazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmazon_Tower_I_topped_out%2C_June_2015.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Amazon%27s_founding_site_in_Bellevue%2C_Washington_-_exterior.jpg/500px-Amazon%27s_founding_site_in_Bellevue%2C_Washington_-_exterior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Amazon%27s_founding_site_in_Bellevue%2C_Washington_-_exterior.jpg/1280px-Amazon%27s_founding_site_in_Bellevue%2C_Washington_-_exterior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Amazon%27s_founding_site_in_Bellevue%2C_Washington_-_exterior.jpg/500px-Amazon%27s_founding_site_in_Bellevue%2C_Washington_-_exterior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","